At Wed, 10 Aug 2005 13:44:53 -0400,
Nambiar, Anil wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
>             I have got alsa driver and aplay up and running on my arm based board. Now
> the AC97 codec on the board is using headphone out instead of speaker out. But the
> ac97 library in alsa is muting headphones and using speaker and phone. I can unmute
> headphone in the driver code and mute speaker and phone, but it is not so elegant. Is
> there any way in the alsa.conf or some other configuration file where I can specify it
> to use headphones instead of speakers? I appreciate for any useful info.

You can call snd_ac97_tune_hardware().  Unmuting is another issue.
It's the policy to mute these volumes per default.


